  "exact_normative_block": "For every assigned proof, enumerate its original logical steps (including unchanged portions) and provide checkable public working for each. A target statement or a bound established inside that same target proof is not an unassigned input. Named UNASSIGNED upstream statements may be used after checking their hypotheses; their own proofs remain unassigned. Reading and reconstruction are distinct: if any required target step is not reconstructed publicly, say so and mark Public reconstruction: PARTIAL or NOT_RECONSTRUCTED, even if Old/New reading is COMPLETE. Do not replace a derivation by saying it is unchanged.",
  "exact_added_output_fields": [
    "- Public reconstruction: COMPLETE | PARTIAL | NOT_RECONSTRUCTED",
    "- Original-step coverage: <steps and working, with omissions explicit>"
  ],
  "rough_word_target": 5000,
  "brevity_instruction": "The word target is approximate; do not sacrifice a required derivation for brevity.",
  "contract_unified_diff": "--- CONTRACT.before.md\n+++ CONTRACT.md\n@@ -10,7 +10,15 @@\n \n This is independent readability-preservation review only, not a Chapter 12 skeptic synthesis, new primary-source theorem-proof/PDF/image verification, Lean quotation, rendered-page, human-signoff, whole-book or release certification. Imported source references remain as stated; inspect the target application under available statements, not an imagined primary-source proof. No prior QA, grades, reports or adjudication is supplied. No tools, shell, network, other files, delegation, edits, contacts or authoring workflow. Only embedded material is allowed. Honest PARTIAL/NOT_READ, uncertainty, refutation or inconclusiveness is permitted. Request only checkable public mathematical deductions, not private reasoning.\n \n+# Public reconstruction requirement\n+\n+For every assigned proof, enumerate its original logical steps (including unchanged portions) and provide checkable public working for each. A target statement or a bound established inside that same target proof is not an unassigned input. Named UNASSIGNED upstream statements may be used after checking their hypotheses; their own proofs remain unassigned. Reading and reconstruction are distinct: if any required target step is not reconstructed publicly, say so and mark Public reconstruction: PARTIAL or NOT_RECONSTRUCTED, even if Old/New reading is COMPLETE. Do not replace a derivation by saying it is unchanged.\n+\n # Output contract\n+\n+Every per-proof section must include these fields in addition to the reading/preservation fields below:\n+- Public reconstruction: COMPLETE | PARTIAL | NOT_RECONSTRUCTED\n+- Original-step coverage: <steps and working, with omissions explicit>\n \n Begin with:\n # Review Result\n@@ -19,4 +27,6 @@\n Verdict: PASS | PASS_WITH_NOTES | FAIL | INCONCLUSIVE\n Confidence: high | medium | low\n \n-Then one ## <proof label> section per inventory label in order. Each gives Old reading COMPLETE|PARTIAL|NOT_READ; New reading COMPLETE|PARTIAL|NOT_READ; Argument preservation PRESERVED|CHANGED|UNCERTAIN; New explanations JUSTIFIED|CONCERN|UNCERTAIN; concrete public calculations and evidence citing equations or view-local LF; lost steps/qualifiers and pre-existing versus new concerns. Explicitly read unchanged proofs; do not substitute hashes for mathematical checks. End with ## Findings and limits. A partially read proof prohibits full-assignment completion. Give exact problematic wording and a bounded correction when justified without inventing a proof. Keep public report roughly 5000 words or less. No broader clearance.\n+Then one ## <proof label> section per inventory label in order. Each gives Old reading COMPLETE|PARTIAL|NOT_READ; New reading COMPLETE|PARTIAL|NOT_READ; Argument preservation PRESERVED|CHANGED|UNCERTAIN; New explanations JUSTIFIED|CONCERN|UNCERTAIN; concrete public calculations and evidence citing equations or view-local LF; lost steps/qualifiers and pre-existing versus new concerns. Explicitly read unchanged proofs; do not substitute hashes for mathematical checks. End with ## Findings and limits. A partially read proof prohibits full-assignment completion. Give exact problematic wording and a bounded correction when justified without inventing a proof. Keep public report roughly 5000 words. No broader clearance.\n+\n+The word target is approximate; do not sacrifice a required derivation for brevity.\n",
